  "goal": "Make the Annihilator 2026 sound like the Annihilator 2023. Built from a same-rig (ATechReviews squig.link, REW/TOPPING Pro) measured difference curve, 2023 minus 2026, L/R averaged and 1 kHz normalized: +3.3 dB bass shelf below ~100 Hz tapering to 0 at 1 kHz (the 2023's bigger low-end weight), +2.9 dB broad presence peak at 4.4 kHz (more forward/energetic upper mids), and a +3.6 dB net air peak at 12.7 kHz with a small 14.8 kHz trim (more EST-tweeter sparkle). Fit below 10 kHz is within ±0.4 dB of the measured difference; the 12-15 kHz region is real but insertion-depth sensitive, so results may vary slightly with tip/fit.",
